Patch 53. After patch 52.

With REXGLUE_ENABLE_PROFILING (every configuration but Release), REX_CALL_INDIRECT_FUNC counted
each indirect call into the perf counter kFunctionsDispatched: rex::perf::IncrementCounter, a call
into the runtime library that is not inlined, doing a relaxed atomic add. The only reader is the
debug overlay's Dispatch line. In Torchlight's fight (fight.txt) that call is about 8 % of the
guest main thread's cycles, so RelWithDebInfo and Debug builds measured a dispatch cost the
release does not have.

The count now needs REXGLUE_PROFILE_INDIRECT_DISPATCH defined as well, as the guest function
zones need REXGLUE_PROFILE_GUEST_FUNCTIONS. Without it the overlay's Dispatch line only counts
FunctionDispatcher::Execute (guest entries from the host). The other counters are unchanged.

Release: REXGLUE_ENABLE_PROFILING is not defined there, so the generated code compiles to the same
thing as before; PGO profiles trained on Release builds still match. The template is one of
codegen_id's inputs, so the id changes and a cross build's host tool must have this patch too.

Measurement: i7-8750H desktop, Torchlight develop b704701, fight.txt offscreen (Xvfb), fps cap 0,
vsync off, no PGO, both builds -O2 -g. perf stat --per-thread on the guest main thread over the
fight step, divided by its frames. A B B A twice, CPU at 2.3-3.4 GHz and 63-84 C at each start
(power profile "performance"), 2026-11-05. Without this patch, RelWithDebInfo against Release:

    cycles/frame  RelWithDebInfo 35.53 M, Release 32.36 M (-8.9 %)
    instructions  RelWithDebInfo 32.99 M, Release 31.06 M (-5.8 %)
    fight mean    13.39 ms against 12.14 ms

perf record of a RelWithDebInfo fight: IncrementCounter, 8 % of the main thread's samples.

With this patch, the same method and machine, both builds against an SDK with the series up to 54
(A B B A twice, 2.4-3.5 GHz and 62-75 C at each start, 2026-11-05):

    cycles/frame  RelWithDebInfo 32.09 M, Release 32.27 M (-0.6 %, RelWithDebInfo the lower)
    instructions  RelWithDebInfo 30.62 M, Release 31.15 M
    fight mean    12.19 ms against 12.33 ms

The two builds' runs overlap (cycles 30.7-32.8 M against 31.3-33.4 M): within the runs' spread.

Upstream: not proposed.

